# Copy this file to .env (git-ignored) for local builds, or set the same
# names as repository *variables* (not secrets - they end up in the public
# client bundle either way) under GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables
# → Actions → Variables, so .github/workflows/static.yml can pass them into
# `npm run build`. See README's "跨裝置同步" and "AI 辨識課表照片" sections
# for what each one is for and how to set up the service behind it.

# Firebase project ID that powers cross-device sync (src/sync.js). Baking
# this in lets every user just enter a pairing code - no Firebase project
# of their own required. Leave unset to fall back to each device typing in
# its own project ID (useful for a fork without its own shared project).
VITE_ORBIT_SYNC_PROJECT_ID=

# Base URL of the deployed Cloudflare Worker (cloudflare-worker/orbit-
# worker.js), e.g. https://orbit-ai-gemini-proxy.<you>.workers.dev - no path
# suffix. This one Worker backs every server-side feature the app has: AI
# schedule-photo import (/gemini), AI natural-language schedule edits
# (/nl-edit, src/editor-nl-edit.js) and cross-device sync (/sync,
# src/sync.js) - each module appends its own hardcoded path (see
# src/proxy-config.js), so there is one URL to set instead of one per
# feature. There is no bring-your-own-key fallback for any of them - a fork
# built from source with no proxy deployed yet just leaves all three
# features unavailable.
VITE_PROXY_URL=

# Optional second Worker deployment (same orbit-worker.js, deployed via
# wrangler.toml's [env.fallback] with Smart Placement deliberately left
# off) that a location-blocked AI request retries against instead of the
# primary Worker again - see README's "AI 辨識課表照片" deployment step 9
# and src/proxy-config.js's proxyFallbackPath for why a plain retry against
# the SAME Worker often lands on the exact same blocked Cloudflare colo.
# Leave unset to keep the weaker (but not broken) fallback of just retrying
# the primary Worker.
VITE_PROXY_URL_FALLBACK=
